top-sort [o_totalprice desc, o_orderdate asc] limit 100
└─ project (c_name, c_custkey, o_orderkey, o_orderdate, o_totalprice, col5) (rows≈3 cost≈13.8K)
   └─ aggregate keys=[customer.c_name, customer.c_custkey, orders.o_orderkey, orders.o_orderdate, orders.o_totalprice] aggs=[sum_0=sum] (rows≈3 cost≈13.6K)
      └─ join inner [orders.o_custkey = customer.c_custkey] emit-filter 1 from left (rows≈3 cost≈13.5K)
         ├─ join inner [lineitem_0.l_orderkey = orders.o_orderkey] emit-filter 2 from right (rows≈3 cost≈9K)
         │  ├─ source lineitem AS lineitem_0 use-filter 2 keys=[lineitem_0.l_orderkey] (rows≈10 cost≈120)
         │  └─ join left_semi [orders.o_orderkey = __qdb_in__] emit-filter 3 from right (rows≈1 cost≈4.6K)
         │     ├─ source orders AS orders use-filter 3 keys=[orders.o_orderkey] (rows≈10 cost≈200)
         │     └─ project (__qdb_in__) (rows≈1 cost≈280)
         │        └─ filter (> sum_0 315) (rows≈1 cost≈276)
         │           └─ aggregate keys=[lineitem_1.l_orderkey] aggs=[sum_0=sum] (rows≈3 cost≈240)
         │              └─ source lineitem AS lineitem_1 (rows≈10 cost≈120)
         └─ source customer AS customer use-filter 1 keys=[customer.c_custkey] (rows≈10 cost≈200)
